            <div xml:id="d219">

                <pb facs="0173" n="164" sameAs="frus:frus1940v02/pg164"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">340.1115A/1439: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Consul General at Marseille</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Hurley</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                        State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Marseille</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1940-08-31">August 31,
                        1940</date>.<lb/>[Received August 31—11:30 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>351. Consulate informed by Commissaire Special at Cerbere Spanish frontier
                    closed. Group of Americans estimated 20 citizens now at Cerbere en route.
                    Barcelona and Lisbon informed. Barcelona wired yesterday frontier situation
                    unclear, apparently now closed to all persons transiting to Portugal. Probably
                    duration situation unknown.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Hurley</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
